<h1>Rossana Rodriguez Sanchez</h1>
<p>33rd Ward alderman, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027. Incumbent.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.rossanafor33.org/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (rossanafor33.org)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Is running for a third term with Chicago DSA&#39;s endorsement, WTTW reported in August 2026, and her campaign is collecting petition signatures to get her on the ballot. Her campaign site points to her record: the CARE Program, Treatment Not Trauma, the Bodily Autonomy and Welcoming City ordinances, the ceasefire ordinance, participatory budgeting and community-driven zoning decisions.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>33rd Ward alderwoman since 2019 and 33rd Ward Democratic committeeperson; former drama teacher in Puerto Rico and resident director of the Albany Park Theater Project.</p>
